(Abstract) Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
14 TL
(Physical activity and sedentary behavior are closely associated with neuropsychiatric ) Tj T*
(diseases, while previous studies have mainly relied on self-reported data, which have been ) Tj T*
(shown to be inconsistent with objectively measured metrics. Using data from 73,411 ) Tj T*
(participants, objectively quantifying physical activity through energy expenditure and time ) Tj T*
(allocation, we identified longitudinal associations between physical activity, sedentary ) Tj T*
(behavior, and neuropsychiatric diseases using Cox proportional hazards models. Our findings ) Tj T*
(indicated that moderate to vigorous physical activity energy expenditure showed the strongest ) Tj T*
(protective effect on neuropsychiatric diseases \(hazard ratios: 0.60-0.86, all FDR-Q < 0.001\), ) Tj T*
(while an increased proportion of sedentary time was identified as a risk factor for ) Tj T*
(neuropsychiatric diseases \(HRs: 1.05-1.54, FDR-Q < 0.05\). Restricted cubic spline analyses ) Tj T*
(demonstrated an L-shaped association linking physical activity and neuropsychiatric diseases ) Tj T*
(and an inverted L-shaped relationship between sedentary behavior and dementia. Linear ) Tj T*
(regression models further linked physical activity and sedentary behavior to cognitive ) Tj T*
(function, physical function, and mental health. Key brain regions related to these behaviors ) Tj T*
(included the lateral occipital cortex, cuneus, pallidum, and accumbens. Proteomics and ) Tj T*
(metabolic analyses identified significant involvement of ITGAV protein and high-intensity ) Tj T*
(lipoprotein. Structural equation modeling elucidated that inflammation and metabolism mediate ) Tj T*
(the relationship between physical activity, sedentary behavior, and neuropsychiatric diseases. ) Tj T*
(Overall, our study provides critical evidence of the link between physical activity, sedentary ) Tj T*
(behavior, and neuropsychiatric diseases, shedding light on potential neurobiological ) Tj T*
(mechanisms underlying these associations.) Tj T*
